#### Example 3: Compound Joints (Coincident Links) {-}


::: {.cell layout-align="center"}
::: {.cell-output-display}
![Example 3 — Planar linkage where links 3, 4, and 5 all share the same revolute joint axis (compound joint). The right-hand detail shows the physical slider-pin arrangement. This compound joint counts as (3-1) = 2 full joints.](images/linkage-ex3-compound-joints.jpg){#fig-ex3-compound-10 fig-align='center' width=90%}
:::
